## The 350-line gate

- No source file exceeds 350 lines, counting neither blank lines nor comment lines.
- ESLint enforces it when the project has the `quality/max-lines` rule (`core/templates/eslint/` in the harness). `node "{{HARNESS_HOME}}scripts/quality-gate.mjs"` uses the same counting method without ESLint, on every `.js`, `.mjs`, `.cjs`, `.jsx`, `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.mts` and `.cts` file outside dependencies and build output. Its scope is wider: the ESLint rule also exempts tests, config and story files, pure re-export modules, and generated or migration directories.
- A legacy file over the limit is recorded as a baseline with its count and date, then reduced in batches. The baseline only moves down.
- Split a large file on a real responsibility seam: logic out of a route, repeated UI into a component, data access into an adapter, a helper cluster into a named module. Keep the public exports stable.

