## Baseline rules

- Strict TypeScript where TypeScript is used, and the framework's official lint presets.
- Server logging goes through the project logger; no direct console output in production code.
- Presentation code does not import the database client.
- Updates and deletes always carry a condition; migrations are reviewed before they run.
- Input and environment are validated at the boundary; errors never contain secrets.

## Feature Map

`.gifisi/feature-map.json` lists every user-visible feature with checks against the live surface (HTTP requests or CLI runs). `node "{{HARNESS_HOME}}scripts/verify-feature-map.mjs"` starts the app, runs each check and exits 1 when any fails. A bug fix adds a check that fails before the fix and passes after it. A new feature adds its entry in the same change.

